HST Office: UserForms as in the file real Excel ran.

The owner's test in real Excel, same route for each: an HST form with TypeInfoVer = 1 in \003VBFrame gives
"The ActiveX Designer's Type Information does not match what was saved", with or without MODULEPRIVATE;
without TypeInfoVer it runs. MS-OVBA gives it as the count of saves of the designer, default 0, and a new
form has none. MODULEPRIVATE is what Office-made form modules have. The caption in the f stream is gone:
real Excel drew it as text inside the form, and the title comes from \003VBFrame in the project's code page.
Controls that name no font now name Tahoma, as Office-made forms do: with an empty name the text sat low and
clipped in real Excel and Word; whether the font alone cures that is being tested.

